#question(title: [A $display(C^oo)$ but not analytic function], shrink: true)[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  Consider the function
  $display(F(x) = cases(e^(-1 \/ x) & quad " if " x > 0 comma, 0 & quad " if " x <= 0 .))$

  + Prove that, for every $n in NN$,
    $display(lim_(t -> oo) t^n e^(-t) = 0)$.
  + Prove that, for every $n in NN$,
    $display(lim_(x -> 0^+) (e^(-1 \/ x))/(x^n) = 0)$.
  + Calculate $display(F' (x))$ for $x > 0$.
  + Calculate $display(F' (x))$ for $x < 0$.
  + Calculate $display(F' (0))$ from the
    definition.
  + Calculate $display(F^(' ') (0))$ from the
    definition.
  + Prove that for every $n in NN$,
    $display(F^((n)) (0) = 0)$.
  + Write the Maclaurin series for $F$ at
    $0$.
  + Is $F$ analytic? Is it $C^oo$?
]
